(7416045, 1169424, 156466, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by PennyStreet:</b></div><hr/><i> In my opinion, this is just as much a double exposure as many of those you commented on. <br/>Beautiful effect though. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Penny, but you and I will have to agree to disagree on the double exposure.  My comments where made when I could distinctly cull out the full details of the "texture" image with that image also lending both new features and distinct features, and adding new image areas - both illegal for a texture according to the rules.  There were many others where I could tell what the image was, but they were used to add texture and not image features.  AS with many of those I may have been heavy handed in my application of the wood grain, but only because the flag exception allowed me to be.</td>', 'Originally posted by PennyStreet: In my opinion, this is just as much a double exposure as many of those you commented on. Beautiful effect though.   Thanks Penny, but you and I will have to agree to disagree on the double exposure.  My comments where made when I could distinctly cull out the full details of the "texture" image with that image also lending both new features and distinct features, and adding new image areas - both illegal for a texture according to the rules.  There were many others where I could tell what the image was, but they were used to add texture and not image features.  AS with many of those I may have been heavy handed in my application of the wood grain, but only because the flag exception allowed me to be.', '2015-11-13 09:17:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(7416048, 1169269, 173844, '<td valign="top">Beautiful image, my personal favorite of the challenge.  Good luck in retaining your ribbon.</td>', 'Beautiful image, my personal favorite of the challenge.  Good luck in retaining your ribbon.', '2015-11-13 10:22:55.000000', NULL, 0),
